<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Steering accuracy (%) across benchmarks. <span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> <math id="S4.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\geq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\geq}</annotation></semantics></math>93%. <math id="S4.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}30</annotation></semantics></math> per cell. IT/base comparison in Table <a href="#S4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 4.5 When does this structure appear? ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Tool Calling is Linearly Readable and Steerable in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07990v1/fig4_emergence.png" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/313;" width="476" height="313" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Mean steering accuracy vs model scale across 3 families. Accuracy rises from 17% (270M) to 89% (27B).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>The model also rewrites its arguments</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">So steering reliably switches the tool name. But what happens to the rest of the output? Something we did not expect is that the model also <em id="S4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">rewrites its entire argument payload</em> to match the new tool’s schema (Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.4 The model also rewrites its arguments ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Tool Calling is Linearly Readable and Steerable in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>):</p>
</div>
