<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Steering accuracy (%, prefix match; see Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Can we exploit this structure to control tool selection? ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Tool Calling is Linearly Readable and Steerable in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> for exact-match analysis on shared-prefix tools). IT / base where both tested. No public Qwen base variants. All <math id="S4.T7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{&lt;}0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{&lt;}0.001</annotation></semantics></math> except <sup id="S4.T7.5" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.T7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> (n.s.). <span id="S4.T7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> <math id="S4.T7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\geq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\geq}</annotation></semantics></math>93%. <math id="S4.T7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}30</annotation></semantics></math> per cell. CIs in Table <a href="#A20.T22" title="Table 22 ‣ Appendix A.20 Full confidence intervals ‣ Tool Calling is Linearly Readable and Steerable in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
